.TH SESSLINT-TRIAGE 1 "" "SessLint 0.4.1" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-triage \- [read\-only] Diagnose a session and explain the next steps.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint triage [\-\-agent {claude,codex}] [\-\-latest] [\-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}] [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-\-policy {conservative,salvage}] [\-\-state\-copy STATE_COPY] [\-\-max\-file\-bytes MAX_FILE_BYTES] [\-\-include\-content] [\-f | \-\-format {human,json}] [\-\-json] [\-o | \-\-output FILE] [\-q | \-\-quiet] [\-v | \-\-verbose] [PATH]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Content\-free evidence and repair previews; never repairs or resumes.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B PATH
Required argument.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-agent {claude,codex}
Choices: claude, codex.
.TP
.B \-\-latest
.TP
.B \-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}
Choices: auto, canonical, claude\-code\-jsonl, codex\-rollout, openai\-agents.
.TP
.B \-\-profile PROFILE
.TP
.B \-\-policy {conservative,salvage}
Explicit salvage opt\-in compares both policies; never acknowledges side effects. Choices: conservative, salvage.
.TP
.B \-\-state\-copy STATE_COPY
Optional closed Codex registry copy outside live agent storage (no WAL).
.TP
.B \-\-max\-file\-bytes MAX_FILE_BYTES
Default: 104857600.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-content
[Invalid for triage] Triage never emits transcript content.
.TP
.B \-f {human,json}, \-\-format {human,json}
Output format (default: human) Choices: human, json.
.TP
.B \-\-json
.TP
.B \-o FILE, \-\-output FILE
Write the report to FILE instead of stdout (existing report files are overwritten atomically)
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error stderr output
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print debug diagnostics (settings provenance, elapsed) to stderr
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1), sesslint\-completion(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

